# aurora.local / packages/ai/pins.env.example
#
# Curated, human-reviewed image pins — the ".example" suffix mirrors the
# existing .env / .env.example convention (see .gitignore): the real
# packages/ai/pins.env is gitignored (generated by `scripts/pin.sh
# --refresh`/`--apply`, host-local), so committed curated recommendations
# live here. Copy or merge into packages/ai/pins.env to adopt.
#
# See dev/notes/pinnable-versions-progress.md for the full inventory and
# reasoning behind every choice in this file.
#
# Once adopted as pins.env, this is consumed by scripts/lib/render.sh
# render_pins() into the environment before `docker compose up`. It only
# takes effect in compose.yml image: lines after `scripts/pin.sh --apply`
# has rewritten them to ${IMAGE_<SVC>} — that has NOT been run.
# compose.yml is untouched by this work.
#
# Format: repo:tag@sha256:digest.
#
# Digests obtained with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}' <ref>

# ollama/ollama — used twice (ollama-cpu, ollama-gpu), same image both
# times. Ollama ships releases roughly every 1-2 days, so the truly
# latest (v0.32.13, one day old at the time of this check) is far inside
# the fortnight caution bar. Went back to v0.32.5 (2026-07-27, ~19 days
# old, stable, not an rc) instead — deliberately not the newest, in line
# with this task's "avoid anything under about a fortnight old" rule.
# Multi-arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm64 — confirmed. Checked 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_OLLAMA_CPU=ollama/ollama:0.32.5@sha256:4dea9fb511947e24a84237bb636b0203abcb2ff0d3fbc7b4ff865deb91362131
IMAGE_OLLAMA_GPU=ollama/ollama:0.32.5@sha256:4dea9fb511947e24a84237bb636b0203abcb2ff0d3fbc7b4ff865deb91362131

# ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui — compose.yml currently pins `:main`,
# which is NOT a release tag, it is the moving development-branch build.
# The project's own docs say explicitly: "avoid the :main tag in
# production, since it tracks the latest development build and can
# introduce breaking changes without warning" and recommend a versioned
# tag instead. Pinned to v0.11.0 (2026-07-27, ~19 days old, stable).
# Worth knowing: earlier v0.9.x releases had a Docker ARM64 reliability
# bug fixed in v0.9.2 — v0.11.0 postdates that fix. Multi-arch:
# linux/amd64, linux/arm64 — confirmed. Note `:main` currently resolves
# to a different, newer digest than v0.11.0, confirming it really is
# tracking unreleased development work, not just a rebuild. Checked
# 2026-08-15.
IMAGE_OPEN_WEBUI=ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui:v0.11.0@sha256:72c0ba641ba75e7aa52655cb242570906ececd09b1140fb736483038a22b3228
